            "scraped_replies": [
                {
                    "is_best": true,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hello,</p>\n<p>It is not available in MX2. It needs to be configured manually in the debug register,<span> </span><strong>DBGMCU_APB1LFZR</strong>, in particular. I invite you to check the reference manual, page 2543.</p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center\" image-alt=\"STackPointer64_0-1776951981484.png\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"STackPointer64_0-1776951981484.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/d94e2f02-6bf3-8fb8-dc51-fb14d3d640ae.png\" title=\"STackPointer64_0-1776951981484.png\"/></span></p>\n<p>Best regards,</p></div>",
                    "author": "STackPointer64",
                    "role": "ST Employee"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Thank you <user-mention data-id=\"93235\">@STackPointer64</user-mention>,</p><p>Much appreciated!</p><p>-Gil</p></div>",
                    "author": "gil_dobjanschi",
                    "role": "Associate III"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hello,</p>\n<p>You need to use <span>DBGMCU block and call call __HAL_DBGMCU_FREEZE_TIMx() to freeze the timer during the debug.</span></p>\n<p><span>If you re using TIM1 so call  __HAL_DBGMCU_FREEZE_TIM1().</span></p>\n<p><span>DBGMCU_APBxy register:</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"mALLEm_0-1776952815071.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"mALLEm_0-1776952815071.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/15afde36-e609-7be5-0cb4-7622f187ebf3.png\" title=\"mALLEm_0-1776952815071.png\"/></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"mALLEm_1-1776952888323.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"mALLEm_1-1776952888323.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a66d1525-d808-39cc-d1b2-f3e315ebe7f7.png\" title=\"mALLEm_1-1776952888323.png\"/></span></p>\n<p><strong>Edit</strong>:</p>\n<p>For <strong>HAL2</strong> use <strong>HAL_DBGMCU_TIM<font color=\"#FF0000\">x</font>_Freeze</strong>() where x is the timer number.</p>\n<p> </p></div>",
